## TeslaSync Apple App — Comprehensive Architecture Map

### **1. NAVIGATION & ROUTING**

**Files & Structures:**
- **`/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260608-002645-33927/slot-622/apps/apple/Sources/App/AppRoute.swift`** (L1-99)
  - Enum defining all 22 top-level routes: `dashboard, vehicles, charging, trips, energy, driving, analytics, maps, vehicleSystems, automations, notifications, telemetry, diagnostics, admin, powerUser, system, settings, onboarding, explore, search, sharing, watch`
  - **`vehicleSystems` DOES NOT have a `/media-player` sub-route yet** — only `.vehicleSystems` exists as a top-level route
  - Route → `LocalizedStringKey` mapping: `LocalizedStringKey("route." + rawValue)` (e.g., `"route.vehicleSystems"`)
  - Icon mapping: `.vehicleSystems` → `"gearshape.2.fill"`
  - Path segment: `.vehicleSystems` → `"vehicle-systems"` (kebab-case conversion via `pathSegment`)
  - Route grouping: `.vehicleSystems` belongs to `.vehicle` group (alongside charging, trips, driving, maps)

- **`/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260608-002645-33927/slot-622/apps/apple/Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift`** (L1-50)
  - `AppRouteParser.parse(path:)` → resolves URL path to route; uses aliases for redirects
  - Aliases (L7-18): `/battery` → `.energy`, `/charging/curves` → `.charging`, `/performance` → `.driving`, etc.
  - No `/media-player` alias currently
  - `AppRouteParser.parse(url:)` handles custom scheme (`teslasync://vehicleSystems`)

- **`/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260608-002645-33927/slot-622/apps/apple/Sources/App/AppShell.swift`** (L1-171)
  - **Route host registration**: `@Environment(\.routeHosts)` holds `AppRouteHostRegistry` (EnvironmentKey)
  - Page rendering happens via `RouteHost` struct (L142-170): calls `routeHosts.view(for: route)` to get registered View or shows `TSEmptyState("route.pagePending")`
  - Adaptive layout:
    - **iPhone compact** (L66-100): `TabView` with primary tabs (dashboard, vehicles, charging, analytics) + "More" tab with remaining routes in sections by group
    - **macOS/iPad** (L39-62): `NavigationSplitView` with sidebar grouping by `AppRouteGroup` + detail stack
  - Sidebar navigation: `List(selection: $selection)` iterates `AppRouteGroup.allCases`, then `AppRoute.routes(in: group)`

- **`/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260608-002645-33927/slot-622/apps/apple/Sources/Platform/Settings/SettingsScene.swift`** (L28-41)
  - Page registration pattern: `registry.register(.settings) { AppSettingsView(...) }`
  - Called from `TeslaSyncApp.body` (L72-75): `environment(\.routeHosts, SettingsRouteRegistration.registry(...))`
