  - `@MainActor @Observable public final class AppContainer` — wires KMP singletons
  - `public var unitPreferences: UnitPreferences` (user's display-unit preferences)
  - `public func model<State>(from flow: Shared.Kotlinx_coroutines_coreStateFlow, transform:...) -> StateHolderModel<State>` — wraps KMP StateFlow into @Observable model
  - `public func loadable<Value>(...) -> StateHolderModel<LoadableState<Value>>` — convenience for Resource<T> → LoadableState<T>

- **`/Users/atulgupta/Documents/repos/.teslasync-parallel/20260608-002645-33927/slot-622/apps/apple/Sources/SharedFacade/Domains/VehicleSettingsModel.swift`** (only example in Domains/)
  - Pattern: feature domain models consume shared core via AppContainer

- **Data fetching pattern (from MediaNowPlayingWidget.Model.swift)**:
  ```swift
  public protocol MediaNowPlayingSource: AnyObject {
      var onUpdate: (@MainActor (MediaNowPlayingUpdate) -> Void)? { get set }
      func start()
      func stop()
      func refresh()
  }
  
  @MainActor @Observable
  public final class MediaNowPlayingModel {
      public enum Phase: Equatable { case loading, empty, error(String), content }
      public private(set) var phase: Phase = .loading
      public private(set) var media: MediaNowPlaying?
      private let source: any MediaNowPlayingSource
  }
  ```
  - View binds to `model.phase` and `model.media`, calls `model.start()/stop()` in `.task`/`.onDisappear`

- **SI Conversion API (Units+Facade.swift L53-100+)**:
  ```swift
  public enum Units {
      public static func convertDistance(_ meters: Double, _ prefs: UnitPreferences) -> Double
      public static func convertSpeed(_ mps: Double, _ prefs: UnitPreferences) -> Double
      public static func formatDistance(_ meters: Double?, _ prefs: UnitPreferences) -> String
      public static func formatSpeed(_ mps: Double?, _ prefs: UnitPreferences) -> String
      // ... more conversions
  }
  ```
  - All math in KMP core (`Shared.UnitsKt.convertDistanceFromSI`, etc.); Swift is a thin bridge
  - UnitPreferences holds display labels: `"km"`, `"mph"`, `"°C"`, `"kPa"`, `"Wh"`, `"h"`, `"W"`

- **Media domain in Shared core:**
  - Shared types: `MediaSnapshotInput`, `MediaVehicle`, `MediaTrackInput` (inferred from widget models)
  - No explicit domain file in `SharedFacade/Domains/` yet (only VehicleSettingsModel.swift present)
  - Production implementation would be: KMP `MediaStore` state holder → `AppContainer.model()` → `@Observable` wrapper for page

